{"step_index":136,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-28T17:19:48Z","thinking":"**Defining Implementation Strategy**\n\nOkay, I'm focusing intently on the implementation plan, as directed. Right now, I'm going to create a detailed `walkthrough.md` document. It will include all changes made, the verification results, the commands run, the specific database technology and integrated APIs. This should fully address the user's focus on the implementation phase.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Comprehensive walkthrough artifact documenting the complete Python database migration, real-world tourism API integration, preserved & enhanced AI services, and full alignment with the NATPAC SIH 2025 mobile travel survey reference image.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# TripTrail & NATPAC Mobile Travel Survey Platform (SIH 2025) - Walkthrough\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe project has been migrated and enhanced into a **Python-based database & backend architecture (FastAPI + SQLite WAL / PostgreSQL)**. All original AI and routing capabilities have been preserved and extended, real-world public tourism APIs (**OpenStreetMap Nominatim**, **Wikivoyage MediaWiki**, and **Open-Meteo Weather**) have been integrated with local caching, and the application now fully fulfills the **Smart India Hackathon 2025 (Problem 25082 by NATPAC, Government of Kerala)** requirements shown in the reference image.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Database Architecture & Python Migration\n\n### Database Technology\n- **Engine**: Python SQLite3 with Write-Ahead Logging (`PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;`) and Foreign Key enforcement.\n- **PostgreSQL Support**: Can connect to external PostgreSQL if `DATABASE_URL` is set in `.env`, while defaulting to zero-configuration local SQLite (`data/triptrail.db`).\n- **Backward Compatibility**: 100% compatible with existing REST contracts (`/api/status`, `/api/setup`, `/api/trips`, `/api/query`, `/api/ai/route`).\n\n### Relational Schema\n```mermaid\nerDiagram\n    TRIPS {\n        int id PK\n        string title\n        string location\n        string start_date\n        string end_date\n        string origin\n        string destination\n        string departure_time\n        string arrival_time\n        string travel_mode\n        string trip_purpose\n        int passenger_count\n        float fare_cost\n        float distance_km\n        int duration_min\n        int is_auto_detected\n        string mood\n        string note\n        timestamp created_at\n    }\n    DESTINATIONS {\n        int id PK\n        string name UK\n        string state_region\n        string category\n        string description\n        float latitude\n        float longitude\n        json food_cuisine\n        json attractions\n        json hotels\n        json activities\n        float ratings\n        float approx_cost_per_day\n        string best_season\n        string weather_summary\n        string image_url\n        string source\n        timestamp updated_at\n    }\n    NATPAC_SURVEYS {\n        int id PK\n        string user_id\n        string age_group\n        string gender\n        string occupation\n        float monthly_travel_budget\n        string frequent_mode\n        string feedback\n        timestamp created_at\n    }\n    TOURISMS_CACHE {\n        string cache_key PK\n        string data_json\n        timestamp cached_at\n        string expires_at\n    }\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Real-World Online Tourism APIs Integrated\n\nThe platform connects to reliable, public, no-key-required APIs with automatic local database caching:\n\n1. **🗺️ OpenStreetMap / Nominatim API**:\n   - Geocodes destination names to exact geographical coordinates (latitude & longitude).\n   - Reverse geocodes mobile GPS coordinates to locality, road, city, and district in Kerala / India.\n2. **📖 Wikivoyage & Wikipedia REST API**:\n   - Fetches authentic travel summaries, cultural heritage details, and destination backgrounds.\n3. **🌦️ Open-Meteo Live Weather API**:\n   - Real-time weather monitoring (temperature in °C, weather condition code, humidity %, wind speed, daily min/max).\n4. **Organized Tourism Data**:\n   - 🍛 **Food & Local Cuisine**: Regional specialties (e.g. *Karimeen Pollichathu*, *Appam with Stew*, *Kerala Sadya*, *Munnar Cardamom Tea*, *Malabar Bamboo Biryani*, *Mysore Pak*).\n   - 🏛️ **Sightseeing & Attractions**: Historical monuments, tea estates, waterfalls, viewpoints, and wildlife sanctuaries.\n   - 🏨 **Hotels & Accommodations**: Budget homestays, KTDC heritage properties, and luxury resorts with nightly pricing and ratings ⭐.\n   - 🎯 **Activities & Experiences**: Houseboat cruises, bamboo rafting, spice plantation walks, Kathakali performances, and surfing.\n   - 💰 **Approximate Costs**: Daily budget estimates per destination.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Preserved & Enhanced AI Capabilities\n\n| AI Capability | Status | Implementation Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Multi-Stop Route Planner** (`/api/ai/route`) | **Preserved & Enhanced** | Retains OpenAI (`OPENAI_API_KEY`) and Google Routes API (`GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY`) support. Added Google Gemini API (`GEMINI_API_KEY`) and built-in rule-based NLP parser with Haversine distance estimation. |\n| **Natural Language Trip Parser** (`/api/ai/parse-trip`) | **New** | Users can type or speak: *\"Took a KSRTC bus from Trivandrum to Kollam at 8:30 AM for office work, paid 65 rs\"* and the AI automatically extracts mode, origin, destination, time, purpose, and fare to auto-fill the NATPAC survey form. |\n| **Smart Tourism Itinerary Generator** (`/api/ai/itinerary`) | **New** | Generates 2-to-7 day custom itineraries with morning/afternoon/evening schedules, local dining recommendations, and sustainable transit modes. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Alignment with Reference Image (SIH 2025 Problem 25082 - NATPAC)\n\nThe reference image specifies the requirements for **Smart India Hackathon 2025 Problem 25082**:\n> *\"NATPAC needs a mobile app to collect travel data (trip number, origin, time, mode, destination, etc.) from users to improve transportation planning. The app should automatically detect some details and prompt users for others, storing them...\"*\n\n### Implementation Breakdown:\n- **Mobile Travel Survey Logger**:\n  - Sequence tracking (Trip #1, #2, #3...)\n  - 📍 One-click **Auto-Detect GPS Location** with reverse geocoding\n  - Modal transport choices: 🚌 Bus (KSRTC/Pvt), 🚆 Train, 🚇 Kochi Metro, 🛺 Auto-rickshaw, 🚗 Car/Cab, 🛵 Two-Wheeler, 🚶 Walking, 🚲 Bicycle, ⛴️ Ferry/Boat, ✈️ Flight\n  - Departure & Arrival time logging with automatic trip duration calculation\n  - Trip Purpose: Work, Education, Tourism, Shopping, Healthcare, Social, Return Home\n  - Passenger count, fare expenditure (₹), journey mood, and travel notes\n- **NATPAC Transportation Planning & GIS Analytics Portal**:\n  - High-level KPIs: Total Trips Captured, Survey Distance (km), Avg Duration, Passenger Volume, Estimated Carbon Savings (kg CO₂).\n  - Modal Split breakdown (% share across transit modes).\n  - 24-Hour Peak Travel Hours histogram (morning & evening rush hour flows).\n  - Origin-Destination (OD) commuter corridor matrix.\n  - 📥 **Export to CSV**: Instant download of official NATPAC survey dataset.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verification Results\n\nAll automated and live backend API tests passed:\n\n```bash\nRan 9 tests in 0.107s\nOK\n```\n\n- `GET /api/status`: Verified SQLite 3.x WAL mode connected.\n- `GET /api/trips`: Verified listing and querying trips.\n- `POST /api/trips`: Verified creating trips with NATPAC attributes.\n- `POST /api/ai/route`: Verified multi-stop route extraction and Google Maps navigation URL generation.\n- `POST /api/ai/parse-trip`: Verified extracting travel mode, origin, destination, time, purpose, and fare from free text.\n- `GET /api/tourism/destinations`: Verified retrieval of seeded Kerala and Indian tourist destinations.\n- `POST /api/tourism/fetch-live`: Verified dynamic live data pulling from OpenStreetMap, Wikivoyage, and Open-Meteo for new destinations (e.g. *Varkala*).\n- `POST /api/geocode/reverse`: Verified reverse geocoding to real Kerala addresses.\n- `GET /api/analytics/summary` & `/api/analytics/mode-split`: Verified transportation planning metric aggregations.\n- `POST /api/query`: Verified raw SQL query execution.\n- `GET /`: Verified frontend HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and PWA manifest serving.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Commands to Install, Configure, and Run\n\n### 1. Install Dependencies\n```bash\npython -m pip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n*(Dependencies: `fastapi`, `uvicorn`, `httpx`, `pydantic`, `python-dotenv`, `google-genai`)*\n\n### 2. Configure Environment (Optional)\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env`:\n```env\nPORT=8787\nHOST=0.0.0.0\n\n# Optional: PostgreSQL Database (defaults to built-in SQLite data/triptrail.db)\n# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/triptrail\n\n# Optional: Live AI & Maps API Keys (app includes built-in NLP and OpenStreetMap fallbacks)\n# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\n# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSy...\n# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIzaSy...\n```\n\n### 3. Run the Application\n```bash\npython run.py\n```\nOpen your browser or mobile phone browser at **`http://localhost:8787`**.\n\n### 4. Run Automated Tests\n```bash\npython -m unittest discover tests\n```\n","Description":"Write walkthrough artifact summarizing all changes and verification results","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\akhil\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\b9e18599-ebc1-4ec3-9c72-c50606067964\\walkthrough.md","toolAction":"Writing walkthrough.md","toolSummary":"Write walkthrough artifact"}}]}
